                <pb facs="0784" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7465a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-01T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1526. Press reports that French have threatened their Black Sea fleet will take
                    action against Soviet Russia unless all French prisoners in Russia are
                    repatriated by October 1st and that wireless message from Moscow quotes
                    Chicherin as saying “We bow to brute force”.</p>
                <pb facs="0785" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/>
                <p>Inquire at Foreign Office concerning alleged French threat and cable all possible
                    facts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
